! N.frr — Stub AS, customer of E
!
! N has a single upstream connection to provider E (10.1.9.2).
!
! As a stub, N:
!   - Announces only its own prefix (10.255.14.1/32) to E via the 'network' statement.
!   - Accepts all routes from E for global reachability.
!   - Provides no transit to any other AS.
!
! Money logic: N pays E for transit. E in turn pays C for global reachability,
! and peers with D to reach D's customers cheaply. N benefits from both paths
! without needing to understand the upstream relationships.

route-map FROM-PROVIDER permit 10
 set local-preference 100
!
router bgp __ASN__
 address-family ipv4 unicast
  neighbor 10.1.9.2 route-map FROM-PROVIDER in
 exit-address-family
!
